# Normalise line endings, so a clone on Windows does not rewrite every file.
#
# Without this, Git's autocrlf setting converts LF to CRLF in the working tree, and every file shows
# as modified the moment Git touches it — which makes a real change impossible to spot in a diff.
# These files are read by Node on every platform; LF is the form that behaves identically.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.apk binary
*.jar binary
*.idsig binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
